{
  "name": "core-comments-beside",
  "description": "Comments on a table, D103's step 4: every write beside the row (D77's primitive 1), so a post moves no version of the row and asks no other behavior's guard, another principal posting while one holds the row's lease, its holder posting without the token its lease requires, and a precondition presented to a post refused; a moderator editing another's message; code blocks held to their own checks and the config's kinds, an attachment block among the kinds (D154); and the config members a table's Comments waits for refused at define, and an attachment scheme that runs code. Cases written by hand in the recorded format, since the engine's recordings hold none of a table's. Each answer holds what the replayer compares: a record's id, data and behaviors, an operation's result, and a refusal whole, in the core's words; what only the engine's store answers (sequence numbers, versions, timestamps, the document a define echoes) is left out.",
